        "math_academy_id": "q-131518",
        "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(0.1<Z<1.5).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.5040\\,$ | $\\,0.5080\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5398\\,$ | $\\,0.5438\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9192\\,$ | $\\,0.9207\\,$ | $\\,0.9222\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9332\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5000\\,$ | $\\,0.5040\\,$ | $\\,0.5080\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5398\\,$ | $\\,0.5438\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9192\\,$ | $\\,0.9207\\,$ | $\\,0.9222\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9332\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ |",
        "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.1<Z<1.5).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/806631e940119accaf9fa2dd9e52e59f4ae16480f237c2bb67ddc7796e4967c0.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.1<Z<1.5) & =P(Z<1.5)-P(Z\\le 0.1) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.5)-P(Z\\le 0.1) \\\\  & =\u03a6(1.5)-\u03a6(0.1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(0.1) & =0.5398 \\\\ \u03a6(1.5) & =0.9332\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.1<Z<1.5) & =\u03a6(1.5)-\u03a6(0.1) \\\\  & =0.9332-0.5398 \\\\  & =0.3934.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
